 "result": "**112 days** passed between the first order (order 6, 2026-07-21) and the last (order 10, 2026-11-10).\n\nOne order's date is stored in a different format from the rest. Order 4 is written as `12/10/2026` while the others use `YYYY-MM-DD`, so SQLite couldn't read it and the plain MIN/MAX query gave the wrong result. I worked out the answer from the full list of dates instead.\n\nThat date could mean two things, but it doesn't change the answer here:\n- **12 October 2026** (day/month order, which fits the shop's euro totals): this falls between the other dates, so the answer stays 112 days.\n- **10 December 2026** (US month/day order): this is after today (2026-11-14), so it can't be right. If it were, the gap would be 142 days.\n\nYou may want to rewrite order 4's date as `2026-10-12` so date queries work correctly.",
